gated. The Done-when digest a record binds is unmoved by a tick or evidence on a Done-when item, so neither unbinds the record.\"","+code_symbol = \"_own_changes/_close_homes/_regenerated/_is_home/build_paths/binding_problem/_unbound/record_problems/_reviewed_problems/_critique_problems/blocking_ids/_cap_problems/_dismissals/_record_lines/commit_lines/_parents/lane_rider/landing_refusal/_squash_lines/_claim_base/staged_lines/main/plan_dir/plan_path/record_path/critique_path/critique_round/bytes_digest/delta/parse/render/blob/plan_digest/done_when_digest/planmode/gate_rows/_unattributed_squash\"","+detail = \"The gate reads only rows claimed by the lane's own active folder at the claim base. The closed planmode set is absent, empty, none, single and dual: absent, empty, none and dual are not gated; single is gated; every other normalized value, and a value that is not a string, is held by name. The closed pre-record change set is the record homes and a close: plan records, review records, decision records, session logs, log fragments, the claimed row's own specification, that specification's move to a closed folder with its report and byte-exact inbound-link redirects, or, as a merge's own changes, the compiled change log and the views the trunk regeneration list names; every other own change is build output. Build output is refused unless a parent holds a pass record binding the row, plan digest and Done-when digest left by the change. A changed pass record is accepted only against its first parent when its nine-key grammar is complete, its delta is none or within and is the plan's own line, its digests match the parent's plan and Done-when, its cited critique is byte-identical in that parent, bound to its reviewed commit and accepted by the verdict grammar, and its dispute pair is both present or both empty; a cited critique record is only round one or round two, and any other round is no record. A second-round non-approval additionally requires an accepted dispute