{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L5Ma3auwxrVVzu2zSGaQNQ","type":"tool_result","content":"status = \"Drafted\"\nstatus = \"Drafted\"\n docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml | 2 +-\n docs/test/test-cases.toml                     | 2 +-\n 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)\n-status = \"Drafted\"\n+status = \"Approved\"\n-status = \"Drafted\"\n+status = \"Approved\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml [('LLR-339', 'status')]\r\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml [('TC-369', 'status')]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73ae5cf9-d335-4bb7-a08f-7631da597f26","uuid":"a632f514-87a8-4dc0-ae70-9bf94d99c59a","timestamp":"2026-10-19T21:52:51.687Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"status = \"Drafted\"\nstatus = \"Drafted\"\n docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml | 2 +-\n docs/test/test-cases.toml                     | 2 +-\n 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)\n-status = \"Drafted\"\n+status = \"Approved\"\n-status = \"Drafted\"\n+status = \"Approved\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml [('LLR-339', 'status')]\r\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml [('TC-369', 'status')]","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-925\\docs\\requirements\\low-level-requirements.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":3478,"oldLines":6,"newStart":3478,"newLines":6,"lines":[" detail = \"The integration branch is named by one declaration in the policy home, read by every reader that needs the trunk. A checkout on that branch is the trunk whether it is the primary checkout or a linked worktree. The trunk is never inferred from the branch a checkout is on; an absent, non-text or empty declaration, or one that names no local branch, is refused naming the declaration by every reader that judges or writes against the trunk. With an undeclared trunk, path-triggered step selection reads the change as unknown and runs every opted-in step, the readability report skips each declared measure naming the declaration, and the worker preflight's terminal-row check keeps its guard. A scaffold writes the branch it is on into the declaration only in a policy configuration created in the same scaffold run, never an adopter's existing file; in an unborn repository it writes the branch git will create, and when the destination has no repository or is detached, the template's value stays and the scaffold names the line to set. A lane's integration base is its merge base with the declared trunk, in a single checkout as in a linked worktree.\""," rationale = \"A declared name gives every trunk-sensitive route one stable identity; guessing from a checkout lets linked worktrees and single checkouts disagree about the same integration branch.\""," test_refs = \"TC-369\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," component = \"CMP-008\""," phase = 6"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-925\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":3571,"oldLines":5,"newStart":3571,"newLines":5,"lines":[" expected = \"The declared branch is read without consulting the current checkout or worktree list; every absent, non-text, empty or non-local declaration is refused naming the declaration; every reader that judges or writes against the trunk refuses naming the declaration; with an undeclared trunk, path-triggered step selection runs every opted-in step, the readability report skips each declared measure naming the declaration, and the worker preflight terminal-row check keeps its guard; a newly created policy configuration records the branch the scaffold is on, including the branch git will create in an unborn repository, while an existing file, no repository, or detached destination retains the template value and names the line to set; a linked worktree on the declared branch is trunk while another branch is not; and a change with no claim copy is not refused over the declara